# G024 — Quote Tracker

*v2. See `quote-tracker.md` for prose: curated collection beyond CRUD,
multi-label tags, first non-deterministic function (nondeterminism as
seed of agency), attribution as provenance.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Domain-Specific Knowledge Curation

[knowledge-curation
    IN ORDER TO
        let each agent curate domain-specific quotes into one shared tracker
        query by tag for a domain view without moving the data
        and surface a random quote constrained by category on demand

    @tracker <- [quotes[new]]

    concurrent [
        sylvia:
            [quotes[add {tracker: @tracker,
                          text: "Kill your darlings.",
                          author: "Faulkner",
                          tags: ["writing", "craft"]}]]
    |
        kathryn:
            [quotes[add {tracker: @tracker,
                          text: "The trend is your friend.",
                          author: "market adage",
                          tags: ["trading", "risk"]}]]
    |
        eliana:
            [quotes[add {tracker: @tracker,
                          text: "Make it work, then make it right.",
                          author: "Kent Beck",
                          tags: ["engineering", "craft"]}]]
    ]
    join

    sync @daily-events {
        morning-wisdom @category ->
            @q <- [quotes[random-by-tag
                            {tracker: @tracker, tag: @category}]]
            [ui[show-morning {quote: @q}]]
    }
]

---

## Verb Surface

[quotes
    new
    add                 {tracker, text, author, tags}
    search-by-tag       {tracker, tag}              ;; multi-label
    search-by-author    {tracker, author}
    random              {tracker}                    ;; nondeterministic
    random-by-tag       {tracker, tag}               ;; constrained random
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: multi-label `where` one quote lives in many sets

[quotes[search-by-tag {tracker: @t, tag: @g}]
    @t:quotes
        where @g is in quote:tags
    IN ORDER TO
        support the real shape of the noosphere — entities with
        multiple facets, multiple memberships, multiple roles —
        rather than single-dispatch classification
]

Tags are sets, not labels. A quote tagged ["craft", "writing",
"wisdom"] belongs to every set simultaneously. Same primitive
underlies G093's tag store and G076's bookmarks.

## Distinctive Innate idiom: nondeterminism as a first-class `where` primitive

[quotes[random-by-tag {tracker: @t, tag: @g}]
    IN ORDER TO
        pick one quote from a constrained pool where neither the caller
        nor the inputs decide which quote is returned

    @candidates <- @t:quotes where @g is in quote:tags
    @candidates
        where count is at least 1  -> select one uniformly at random
        otherwise                   -> none
]

First resolver verb that returns different results for the same
input — the seed of agent autonomy. Agents making choices not
dictated by their inputs IS nondeterminism.

---

## Demo

[demo
    @t <- [quotes[new]]
    [quotes[add {tracker: @t, text: "In the beginning",
                  author: "Genesis", tags: ["wisdom", "origin"]}]]
    [quotes[add {tracker: @t, text: "Premature optimization...",
                  author: "Knuth", tags: ["engineering", "wisdom"]}]]

    -> [quotes[search-by-tag {tracker: @t, tag: "wisdom"}]]
    ;; -> both quotes

    -> [quotes[random {tracker: @t}]]
    ;; -> one of them, different on successive calls
]
